A1. These spin rattling good tails. ~ RATTLESNAKES
A12. Here's a good place to get in the soup. ~ TUREEN
A13. Harlem tint. ~ SEPIA
A16. To bring on a shotgun wedding. ~ BETRAY
A18. Little skirts. ~ GIRLS
A20. The middle of Dora. ~ OR
A22. English counties. ~ SHIRES
A24. Famous heart specialist. ~ CUPID
A26. Salve for a conscience. ~ SOP
A28. Good prison for slippery customers. ~ EELPOT
A30. Russell's meal ticket. ~ PETE
A31. Go signal on a couch. ~ QUIT
A33. The kind of missionaries most welcome on Cannibal Isle. ~ FAT
A35. Food for a wise cracker. ~ NUT
A36. This is the best way to loosen up. ~ UNTIE
A38. How persistent spinsters land their catches. ~ RETRAP
A41. Not quite a finished ark. ~ AR
A42. This is a sentimental composition in music. ~ IDYLL
A43. An island where knights were bold. ~ MALTA
A45. Half a "Thank you!" ~ TA
A46. These animals are most dangerous when blind. ~ TIGERS
A50. A fellow who lives with a nag. ~ STOIC
A51. This marks the waistline in Yokohama. ~ OBI
A53. The river on which the Swiss navy maneuvers. ~ AAR
A54. Voracious coin-eater. ~ SLOT
A55. How long does it seem since the good old days? ~ EONS
A57. Night buzzer. ~ SNORER
A61. This is a cuckoo in South America. ~ ANI
A62. Susan—before she grew up. ~ SUSIE
A64. The man with an eye for figures. ~ SUMMER
A66. Just like that. ~ SO
